Arm T's two page-level probes are decided, and both point the same way: the long-chunk model's loss comes in at stage 2 (training on page images) or later, not at stage 1 (text-only pretraining). Four follow-up cells are queued, and the campaign wakes again when they finish (3 hours at most).

## What decided this wake
The question for this probe set is why the model pretrained on 1,024-token chunks (call it L1024) answers worse than the one pretrained on 256-token chunks (C256).

| Probe | Data | Metric | C256 | L1024 | Gap (95% CI) | Gate |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Page transcription: rebuild the answer page from its compressed slots. Stage-2 models. | 500 pages | share of the page's words rebuilt (higher is better) | .647 | .566 | −8.0 pt [−10.6, −5.5], p 4e-16 | met |
| Text rebuild of one 256-token chunk. Stage-1 models. | 500 unseen documents | nats per token (lower is better) | .0144 | .0126 | −.0018 [−.0031, −.0006] | not met: L1024 is not worse |

- **Transcription:** L1024's compressed page slots really hold fewer of the page's words. All three document sources go the same way. There is one stage-2 model per chain, so no second seed exists for this probe.
- **Stage-1 rebuild:** both models rebuild short text chunks almost perfectly. The control (rebuilding from another document's slots) is far worse, and a model paired with itself gives 0, so the probe is working.
- **Together:** long chunks in stage 1 did not cost short-chunk skill at stage 1. The loss shows up after stage 2. All of this is still marked provisional until the next verifier pass.

## Running now
- **Text, three cells:** ten short HotpotQA passages on the three remaining fine-tuned models (L1024 seed 42, C256 seed 43, L1024 seed 43), about 22 minutes each. The fourth (C256 seed 42) is done: judge accuracy .579 on 1,500 questions, healthy.
- **Text rebuild on the stage-2 models:** a new cell. It tells whether stage 2 also lost text detail or only page-image detail. I wrote its pass/fail rule into the campaign rules before launching. To run it, I added a model-set option to the campaign's own rebuild launcher. The default behaviour is unchanged.

## Bookkeeping
- Updated `docs/longdoc_diagnosis.md` with a new table of these probe results.
- Saved both comparison tables under `expQ/longdoc/`.
- Recorded verdicts and rewrote the campaign state file.
- Cells used: 27 of 70. GPU-hours: about 12.4 so far.
- The campaign results page still shows 0 rows even though the results table has them. This is a known, already-reported expmon bug, so I filed nothing new.

